## Context

The highest-yield part of the backlog: status series over time are what
observations and timings are made of. Scope, before dedup: progress updates 24
(VNM 14, ZAF 9, SEN 1), annual reports 7 (ZAF 4, SEN 3), operator reports 8
(IDN 6, SEN 1, ZAF 1) and project lists 8 (ZAF 5, SEN 2, VNM 1). 1501 removes
duplicates and translations first. Some are Vietnamese (`vi`) or French.

## Method (author decision, 2026-09-29)

- Where a publisher repeats one format (for example the 14 VNM progress
  updates), one purpose-built parser writes the lines of the whole series;
  the parser is the artifact, its output is reviewed as a diff.
- One-off PDFs: LLM-assisted reading with row-by-row diff review, at a stated
  budget. `decided_by` names the model.
- Each document gets a `line-field-specs` row at extraction; the field file
  header is validated against it.
- Lines only in this ticket. Observations follow the storage contract rules and
  cite the lines; no referent or project is minted here beyond what
  [[0875]]'s tables already hold.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every document cleared by 1501 for this wave has lines, or a recorded disposition with the reason
- [ ] Lines of the 254 previously extracted documents are byte-identical before and after
- [ ] Each parser has a test on a fixture drawn from a real snapshot, and was red-tested by replaying a defect it must reject
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, `make check-fast`, `make lint` and `make check-jetp` pass
- [ ] New counts by country and document type stated in the PR
- [ ] `sen-senelec-procurement-2026` (Senelec notice index) has lines, so the Saloum AAO 30/2026 index date 09/09/2026 is a cited line for `sen-project-annex-16-procurement-2026-09-09` (ticket 1590, log note 2026-09-29)
